e summer and he was going to be  you know focusing on rational choice  Theory Aristotelian Thomism and Freud  and Lacan and I was like oh I'm gonna  apply for that definitely so I did and I  got hit I was the most junior scholar  involved in that there were 10 of us who  got selected and they put us up at Notre  Dame and fed us and then each day we  would meet with MacIntyre in these  seminars and you know we had to do  projects of our own and had the  opportunity to interact with him  afterwards and MacIntyre you know he's a  guy who does virtue ethics and he's  somebody who not just talks the talk but  really really really walks the walk very  much so he comes out of an old Marxist  tradition eventually you know becomes an  Aristotelian that an Augustinian that  it's homeless you know becomes a  Catholic along the way does some very  interesting work and I remember I would  see him that at you know conferences and  he would come up and he'd just start  chatting and here's the one thing that  you can say about MacIntyre and you can  say about many of these other people  who've been in port  teachers for me he's not what in  biblical terms you would call a  respecter of persons that is somebody  who really cares about the rank or the  prestige of somebody and isolates  themselves off with that person and  ignores everybody else McIntyre does the  opposite as a matter of fact I don't  know if he's still teaching at this time  at Notre Dame but at the time that I was  interacting him with him fairly  regularly  he was only teaching undergraduates even  though he could if he wanted just he's  graduate students and just teach the  subjects he wanted he was teaching core  classes because he said these are the  most important students these are the  most important classes again somebody  who made a very big impression on me so  all of these people I would say are in  some sense responsible for you know  better or worse the kind of guy I've  become I've drawn a lot of lessons from  them some of which have articulated to  you many of which I don't even know if I  could articulate to myself because  that's the way people make impressions  upon us but I wanted to honor each and  every one of them during this this week  devoted to you know honoring teachers  for the work that they do so there you  have it those are you know the people  who've made the biggest impression on me  through their teaching  you
 

